Windows Event IDs — SOC Analysis
1. Event ID 4624 — Successful Logon

Meaning: A user/account successfully logged into Windows.

Your lab shows:

Log: Security
Event ID: 4624
Level: Information
Task Category: Logon
Keywords: Audit Success
Description: An account was successfully logged on.

SOC analyst thinking:

"Who logged in? When? Was this login expected?"

A 4624 event by itself is not an attack. The analyst checks the surrounding information and other events to determine whether the login is legitimate.

Remember:

4624 = SUCCESSFUL LOGIN ✅
